<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugippius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 465–c. 533</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugippius was a monk and disciple of Saint Severinus, who left Noricum with the Roman population in 488 and became abbot of a monastery near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. Around 511 he wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/life-of-saint-severinus">Life of Saint Severinus</a>, a vivid account of the last years of Roman rule on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. It is the main source for the Rugians and their kings.</p></div>
